<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SAND_SWIMMERS_MOD_1 — the item half of the sand-swimmer family: the catch
  (RSW_DuneCrawler) and the rare prize (RSW_GlassPearl). The predator half
  (RSW_SandStalker, "the thing that catches the catcher") is a live creature —
  see ThingDefs_Races/RSW_SandStalker.xml — and enters the loop as a rare catch
  corpse via ThingSetMakerDefs/RSW_RareSandCatches.xml, not as an item here.

  PRECEDENT CHECK (done before designing, per the item's own instruction):
  - "sand prowler burrow-swim precedent" — CONFIRMED REAL. Alpha Animals' AA_SandProwler
    (`sarg.alphaanimals`) fakes "burrows in sand" with zero C#, via VEF's
    `CompProperties_GraphicByTerrain` (swaps to a `_Hidden` graphic while standing on
    listed sand terrains) + hediff `AA_BurrowingUnderSand`. Full technical writeup:
    design/Jawa/worldbuilding/desert_ecology_feasibility.md §7 and §9. This mod does
    NOT reuse that comp (see RSW_SandStalker.xml header for why), but the precedent is
    real and is where the "sand-swimmer" vocabulary in this campaign comes from.
  - "Blue Desert's sand-swimmer gene" — the ITEM's citation is WRONG ABOUT THE BIOME,
    though the gene itself is real. Gene A26 "Sand-swimmer" ("+0.5 move on sand, no
    footprints there") lives in `design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_slime_gene_lists.md`
    — THE SLIME's gene-machine roster, riders picked up from visitors to that biome —
    not in `the_blue_desert.md`, which has no "sand-swimmer" or "sand-swim" text at all
    (checked directly). Flagging this rather than silently repeating the item's claim.

  NEVER FISH-SHAPED (owner's explicit instruction): both items below are armored/
  crystalline analogs, described and iconed accordingly, not as fish.

  ANTI-EXPONENTIAL: Nutrition/MarketValue held at or below vanilla Fish_* tier
  (FishBase: Nutrition 0.25, MarketValue 6.5) — no yield multiplier over ordinary
  fishing. The population cap that actually keeps this a "thin windfall, not a farm"
  lives on the biome side (RUT: Patches/SandFishing_CrackedLands.xml's
  maxFishPopulation), not here.

  ART — PLACEHOLDER for both items (owed, not generated this pass). validate_patch.py
  proved a plain cross-mod vanilla texPath reference does NOT check out here (vanilla
  Core's own art is packed into resources.assets/AssetBundles, not loose PNGs under
  Data/, so this repo's static texture scan can't see it, and this project's own
  convention — RSW_Jerba reusing the already-absorbed Bantha sprite — is to point at
  art that is physically present in THIS mod's own Textures/ folder). Reused instead,
  both confirmed present on disk and both already free of the fish silhouette:
  RSW_DuneCrawler  -> swresource/AbsorbedEggs/RSW_InsectEgg (an egg/chitin read)
  RSW_GlassPearl   -> swresource/Trophies/BanthaHorn (a distinct valuable-prize read)
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="FishBase">
    <defName>RSW_DuneCrawler</defName>
    <label>dune crawler</label>
    <description>A fist-sized, many-legged scavenger with a fused mineral shell, pulled up out of deep sand on a fishing line. It spends its whole life below the surface filtering decayed organics out of the sand — silverbole leaf-fall, dead things the dune swallowed, whatever a wreck sheds — and only ever reaches the light when something eats it or something catches it. Nothing about it says "fish." Cooked, it eats like a shrimp with regrets.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>swresource/AbsorbedEggs/RSW_InsectEgg</texPath>
      <!-- PLACEHOLDER — see header. -->
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
  </ThingDef>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase">
    <defName>RSW_GlassPearl</defName>
    <label>glass pearl</label>
    <description>A smooth, water-clear nodule fused out of silica deep inside a deep-sand pool — kin to the light-pipe nubs that dot the dune sea's surface, but rounder, and rarer, because nothing usually digs this deep to find one. Ash'karr's optics trade calls a good one "a lens that grew a skin." Sold whole, or cut for what's inside.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>swresource/Trophies/BanthaHorn</texPath>
      <!-- PLACEHOLDER — see header. -->
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
    </graphicData>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ResourcesRaw</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>38</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.15</Mass>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>4</Beauty>
      <DeteriorationRate>1</DeteriorationRate>
    </statBases>
    <alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
    <stackLimit>25</stackLimit>
    <tradeability>Sellable</tradeability>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>ExoticMisc</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
